<title>BELGIUM: DEGROOF REITERATES GLAVERBEL A &quot;BUY&quot;.</title>
<headline>DEGROOF REITERATES GLAVERBEL A &quot;BUY&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of research report - </p>
<p>Co name-----------Sector------Price------Broker-------------</p>
<p>Glaverbel			   4,885 *    Bank Degroof</p>
<p>COMMENT: Glaverbel can expect to benefit from higher sales</p>
<p>volumes and prices in coming months. Overall 1997 sales seen up</p>
<p>4.6 pct at 40.4 bln Bfr. Rise in prices expected in July will</p>
<p>reverse 1996 fall in operating margin. Average earnings per</p>
<p>share should rise 43 percent in 1996-1998, helped by lower</p>
<p>gearing.</p>
<p>Recommendation: BUY (rating unchanged since April)</p>
<p>Analyst: Caroline Lauwers (*) Date of report: 19/06/97</p>
<p> Estimates:   EPS	  pvs est   P/E     Dividend</p>
<p> 1996	   205 BFR    n/a	 23.8    140 BFR</p>
<p> 1997	   295 BFR    244 BFR   16.3    128 BFR</p>
<p> 1998	   420 BFR    380 BFR   11.5    148 BFR</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
